{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008513-tragic-fate-of-the-greatest-magical-artisan-ever-graced-the-earth","id":1008513,"title":"Tragic fate of the greatest magical artisan ever graced the Earth","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-26T06:44:18-08:00","id":1008513,"title":"Tragic fate of the greatest magical artisan ever graced the Earth","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the beginning of the ninth century, his ship foundered in a storm off the coast of Corsica and his hereditary enemies, the sons and nephews of the man he had slain many years ago, captured him. Typical of a Corsican vendetta, the murder had not been forgotten.<br /> <br /> Dragging the bound Verditius to the family\u2019s patriarch,<b> t</b><b>he magus was slain, his head and heart removed and his body fed to the crows</b>. </div> </div> </div>So ignominious end for a Hermetic Founder. How a mere<b> mundane Corsican family</b> was able to savage, capture, interrogate and then murder a medieval archmagus, and arguably one of the most potent magi ever lived. Is that even theoretically possible?<br /> <br /> I think it is one of the most absurd, stupid, improbable and most of all contrived event of the Dark Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-26-2016, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T08:30:49-08:00","id":1008555,"title":"","content":"History is not made up of what happened, only of what was recorded to have happened. Perhaps this particular nugget of information is a gross simplification or even an outright lie in order to mislead or discourage others from learning what really happened, and the grave truth it carried.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you can run a game about what &quot;really&quot; happened that day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T08:37:03-08:00","id":1008560,"title":"","content":"Plus, what the Hell, did they want the head and heart <i>for</i>?<br /> <br /> And, if it was me.... I'd take Verditus' <b><i>hands</i></b>....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T09:23:01-08:00","id":1008577,"title":"","content":"His usual defense against such attacks might have been a hostility-removing Corona/Mind spell. The problem being that here the attackers are working as part of a family/regional tradition, in a group, and to avenge a murder committed against one of their own. All of this together would take some successes off the protection.<br /> <br /> He might have been engaging in some rituals or spells that caused him not to recast his protection(s) ; and was caught flat-footed by his ship's accident.<br /> <br /> Other Mages or Nightfolk (including Sorcerers) might have directed the attack, or aided the participants once it took place.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008513-tragic-fate-of-the-greatest-magical-artisan-ever-graced-the-earth?p=1008560#post1008560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, what the Hell, did they want the head and heart <i>for</i>?<br /> <br /> And, if it was me.... I'd take Verditus' <b><i>hands</i></b>....</div> </div> </div> </div>What would you want the hands for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T09:26:33-08:00","id":1008580,"title":"","content":"As if that is not enough, the same 'mundane' family managed to effectively defeat <b>the entire House Verditius</b>, to make matters worse. They fought standstill against full might of the House for 30 years and penetrated Domus Magna of the Verdititus and almost assassinated its Primus and bludgeoned a Hermetic House into humiliating submission AND survived.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gelon assumed the role of Primus of the House, beginning the long tradition of the eldest living filius of the Primus assuming the role upon the leader\u2019s demise. Gelon unwisely sought Verditius\u2019s killers and slew them, unknowingly continuing the blood feud. This was Gelon\u2019s greatest failing, as it perpetuated the vendetta that could have ended with Verditius\u2019s death. It also began a terrible legacy that still poisons the House, although in a much subtler way. Gelon realized his mistake when <b>a group of Corsican assassins penetrated Verdi </b>and tried to kill him. Slaying the assassins only worsened the feud, and Gelon realized that it would only end after the Corsican family had the upper hand. <b>The vendetta lasted for 30 years, flaring up every five years or so</b>, until Gelon magnanimously bestowed the title of Primus on his first apprentice and <b>surrendered to his enemies.</b> </div> </div> </div>Thus, now I wonder whether the family was <i>really </i>mundane or not. It may be possible the said family was actually a powerful Order of Corsican magi. Verdititus' domus magna, Verdi, was located in the Sardinia, after all.<br /> <br /> And if the nearby island was <i>also </i>containing a powerful rival Order of magi, which could utilize entire magick, resource and population of the particular island...<br /> ...Or, the said family was merely a pawn/servant/front/mercenary/slave/whatever of some much, much powerful and insidious force, such as demons, faeries, spirits and/or rival traditions of magi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-26-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T10:24:42-08:00","id":1008596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008513-tragic-fate-of-the-greatest-magical-artisan-ever-graced-the-earth?p=1008577#post1008577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would you want the hands for?</div> </div> </div> </div>The hands of the Primus whose House is known for creating magical artifacts? Sympathetic magic? <br /> <br /> You could probably make up an &quot;organ harvest&quot; list for the Primi of the various Houses pretty easily....<br /> Bonisagus.... head<br /> Verdititus... hands<br /> Flambeau.... spleen (his entire life seemed to be a venting thereof)<br /> Jerbiton.... pneumatic tract (just rip it all out, lungs to lips...)<br /> etc. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T15:13:50-08:00","id":1008687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008513-tragic-fate-of-the-greatest-magical-artisan-ever-graced-the-earth?p=1008577#post1008577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you want the hands for?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Craftsman's hands are his life and his pride. From those hands, spring forth miracles rendered tangible. Even were it not a Magus Craftsman's hands, they represent his art.<br /> <br /> Even if you collect the hands just to have them, they are a trophy of victory against him. Their bones could be mounted in a frame and displayed in the family home.<br /> <br /> Hell, they didn't even necessarily need to kill the Primus. If they chopped off his hands, he might as well be dead. Or at least he would, were he not a wizard, who could either regrow his hands, or direct the forging of fully articulate, magical iron hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T18:29:19-08:00","id":1008732,"title":"","content":"An unfortunately timed Paradox backlash could explain one mage, however powerful, falling to mundane enemies. But that seems a rather less likely explanation for a family successfully pursuing a vendetta against an entire Hermetic house over the course of a generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T18:17:53-08:00","id":1009107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008513-tragic-fate-of-the-greatest-magical-artisan-ever-graced-the-earth?p=1008732#post1008732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An unfortunately timed Paradox backlash could explain one mage, however powerful, falling to mundane enemies. But that seems a rather less likely explanation for a family successfully pursuing a vendetta against an entire Hermetic house over the course of a generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that is an utter bullshit.<br /> <br /> And AFAIK, Paradox did not exist during the Dark Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:45:27-08:00","id":1009437,"title":"","content":"Well, Scourge or whatever it was operating as a limiting force on true magick back then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:15:02-08:00","id":1009451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008513-tragic-fate-of-the-greatest-magical-artisan-ever-graced-the-earth?p=1009437#post1009437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Scourge or whatever it was operating as a limiting force on true magick back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in the DA, there wasn't anything like Scourge or Paradox. Or True vs. Static Magic. It was all just folks and when you fail, you fail. If you botch, like any other botch in any other roll in any other game than Mage, it was up to the ST to make up something appropriate about why that particular failure was nastier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T15:29:18-08:00","id":1009509,"title":"","content":"The easiest explanations are either that the family is supernatural in some way (pick whatever is most interesting for your game) or that House Verditius at the time focused on creation of magical devices so much that they are unable to quickly produce magical effects. In other words, they can only alter local reality via a device and not through Will directly. I can imagine a shipwreck causing a mage to lose his panoply of wondrous items, and without them, he's relatively powerless in the moment. <br /> <br /> It'd be pretty hard to represent that mechanically, especially in Dark Ages: Mage, but it already didn't really work for Verditius unless you assume he had Materia before those *other* guys did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:52:11-08:00","id":1009573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008513-tragic-fate-of-the-greatest-magical-artisan-ever-graced-the-earth?p=1009509#post1009509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest explanations are either that the family is supernatural in some way (pick whatever is most interesting for your game) or that House Verditius at the time focused on creation of magical devices so much that they are unable to quickly produce magical effects. In other words, they can only alter local reality via a device and not through Will directly. I can imagine a shipwreck causing a mage to lose his panoply of wondrous items, and without them, he's relatively powerless in the moment.<br /> <br /> It'd be pretty hard to represent that mechanically, especially in Dark Ages: Mage, but it already didn't really work for Verditius unless you assume he had Materia before those *other* guys did.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always a little amusing to try to square the Hermetic's Dark Age Pillars with the stated specialties of the various constituent Houses....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T02:27:26-08:00","id":1013658,"title":"","content":"Mages are pretty much ordinary humans. You catch them unaware and unprepared, you mangle them and make sure they don't have access to their tools and you can do just fine with murdering them. If that reply is not good enough you can always say they made a dark pact of some kind or used an ancient mcguffin, but that really detracts from the fact that normal people can be quite dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T06:09:11-08:00","id":1013708,"title":"","content":"Yeah, any mage can be caught flat-footed and defeated by a group of mortals in certain situations. I can see how a group of assassins fighting a guerilla campaign could be an issue. I'm not sure if it just Corsicans just running at the front door blindly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T06:25:49-08:00","id":1013714,"title":"","content":"It's as simple as catching him in bed with his favourite courtesan, and beating the crap out of him to knock him out (2-3 men with clubs should suffice) or have the courtesan drug him. After that strip him naked, break his fingers, cut his tongue and possibly even poke out his eyes. You can proceed to torture and mangle him to your own satisfaction.<br /> <br /> Also if popular culture teaches us anything it's that you should never fuck with the Corsicans. Sicilians at least have scruples!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T09:07:19-08:00","id":1015261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008513-tragic-fate-of-the-greatest-magical-artisan-ever-graced-the-earth?p=1013714#post1013714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's as simple as catching him in bed with his favourite courtesan, and beating the crap out of him to knock him out (2-3 men with clubs should suffice) or have the courtesan drug him. After that strip him naked, break his fingers, cut his tongue and possibly even poke out his eyes. You can proceed to torture and mangle him to your own satisfaction.<br /> <br /> Also if popular culture teaches us anything it's that you should never fuck with the Corsicans. Sicilians at least have scruples!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If any sort of experienced mage fell to that crap I would call him an incompetent moron, he deserved it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would you want the hands for? </div> </div> </div>If any of you are interested, there is a fascinated book called The Right Hand of The Grand Master.<br /> A tale of the tribulations of medieval man rebuilding the grandest cathedral of their time, interwoven with mystery plays, prophetic dreams, intrigue and love it makes a great reading. Here are some links:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Right_Hand_of_the_Grand_Master\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ri...e_Grand_Master</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.google.ge/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=2&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiXlaSwjurQAhWJFSwKHVNaAFEQFggeMAE&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fjournal.ibsu.edu.ge%2Findex.php%2Fsjh%2Farticle%2Fdownload%2F519%2F449&amp;usg=AFQjCNG49AGPvVpBiEKEjxdk7hoR7GA6tg&amp;sig2=1mLM0E3vG3sys8UagX0bHw&amp;bvm=bv.141320020,d.d24\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.ge/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j...41320020,d.d24</a></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 12-10-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T19:24:20-08:00","id":1015479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008513-tragic-fate-of-the-greatest-magical-artisan-ever-graced-the-earth?p=1015261#post1015261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If any sort of experienced mage fell to that crap I would call him an incompetent moron, he deserved it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like...<br /> The fire mage that immolated himself? (Flambeau)<br /> <br /> The combat mage who picked a fight no one could win by going off to beat the Fae at their own game, and was never seen again? (Tytalus)<br /> <br /> The mage who burned out is own magic and became a sort of &quot;pet&quot;? (Mercere)<br /> <br /> The seer who got it so wrong that he sort of &quot;vagued&quot; himself out of existence to the level that even his followers, who can know pretty much anything, are very unclear about what happened to him? (Criamon)<br /> <br /> And (drum roll please)<br /> The mage who sensed the coming change in magic but effed up so badly with his solution that he ended turning himself and his entire House into vampires? <br /> <br /> Powerful mages (particularly, apparently, powerful Hermetics) often go down hard and permanently for relatively minor reasons. That's what the the whole &quot;Hubris&quot; meme is about....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T23:51:17-08:00","id":1015575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008513-tragic-fate-of-the-greatest-magical-artisan-ever-graced-the-earth?p=1015479#post1015479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like...<br /> The fire mage that immolated himself? (Flambeau)<br /> <br /> The combat mage who picked a fight no one could win by going off to beat the Fae at their own game, and was never seen again? (Tytalus)<br /> <br /> The mage who burned out is own magic and became a sort of &quot;pet&quot;? (Mercere)<br /> <br /> The seer who got it so wrong that he sort of &quot;vagued&quot; himself out of existence to the level that even his followers, who can know pretty much anything, are very unclear about what happened to him? (Criamon)<br /> <br /> And (drum roll please)<br /> The mage who sensed the coming change in magic but effed up so badly with his solution that he ended turning himself and his entire House into vampires?<br /> <br /> Powerful mages (particularly, apparently, powerful Hermetics) often go down hard and permanently for relatively minor reasons. That's what the the whole &quot;Hubris&quot; meme is about....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> magical mishaps? sure. overreaching? why not. corruption? happens too often. <br /> <br /> all of your examples list causes linked to hubris and magic. not being beat-up by 2-3 mundanes with clubs. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *However... yeah, I don't have very high opinion about any mage on your list either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T01:04:35-08:00","id":1015593,"title":"","content":"I agree with Asmodai and Ajax on this one. While we'd love to be able to say that a Master Mage would be impossible to get the drop on, they are still at their core human beings. It is possible for sleepers to sneak up on a Master unawares while he slumbers, and kill him on the spot.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I find it questionable how a <i>Master</i> could be rendered powerless by removing his tools. Even for the tool-focused Verditus, this seems like a stretch. He only needs to have overcome a single one of his Instruments to turn the entire gang to glass on the spot.<br /> <br /> Killing a Master Mage while he sleeps? Entirely reasonable, assuming the mortals were able to breach any and all magical defenses getting there. Capturing, transporting, and torturing him? That I don't buy. If nothing else, the stress of the situation might cause him to start spitting some powerful freaking Wild Magic, which wouldn't be pleasant for anyone in the immediate radius of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T08:50:41-08:00","id":1015686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008513-tragic-fate-of-the-greatest-magical-artisan-ever-graced-the-earth?p=1015575#post1015575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> magical mishaps? sure. overreaching? why not. corruption? happens too often.<br /> <br /> all of your examples list causes linked to hubris and magic. not being beat-up by 2-3 mundanes with clubs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *However... yeah, I don't have very high opinion about any mage on your list either.</div> </div> </div> </div>They lived centuries. Statistically, something is going to get you in the end. I don't think merely persisting is a cause for a lot of respect. Merinita might still be alive (or not), but off in the Dreaming or something. She's been noted as being the last Founder around. There's no real information about the deaths of some of them, but the implication is that Guernicus, Bonisagus, Jerbiton, or Bjornear. or for that matter, Pralix, Trianoma, Guorna or Diedne. Admittedly, I am not going to to do all the necessary digging, but I'll just let the Merinita factoid (from Ars Magica materials prior to the creation of the WoD) stand in in a place of a of a lot of work. So all of them also failed somehow.... (There is the potential for a lot of good stories in there.... like, was it Bonisagus's immortality potion that failed and caused Tremere to loose his shit? They had worked together closely in creating Certamen, when Tremere was young and Bonisagus was THE MAN, so there might have been some kind of relationship and respect there... And so on...) Is it worth less respect to have a mage die with a bang than a whisper (or an &quot;Exit, Stage Left&quot;)? <br /> <br /> Verditus's death is due to a magical mishap as well. Or the consequences of a magical choice. Which amounts to the same thing. Apparently, he didn't make a &quot;keep me from being beaten to death by Corsican thugs when I am taken unawares&quot; device. Or, if he did, it wasn't on the bedside table when they broke into the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 12-11-2016, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}